{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>As on this day.</b> Meaning, in the order that you are on this day, when the entire congregation was complete and fit, and as He testified concerning them that all of them were cleaved to HaShem etc. — ״חַיִּים״ (Deuteronomy 4:4). And the intention of the statement is that outside this order there is no chosenness in them, even though they may be the seed of the beloved ones — if they act wickedly, their seed is not reckoned. And Ishmael and Esau are a sign for you, for our eyes see that they were the sons of Abraham and Isaac, and even so Scripture said: ״כִּי בְיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זָרַע״ (Genesis 21:12, Nedarim 31a)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:26.794285983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}